# Line endings are part of the source here, not a local preference.
#
# `renderer/index.html` carries an inline boot script, and its exact bytes are
# what the Content-Security-Policy hash in `main/security.ts` is computed over.
# A checkout that swapped LF for CRLF — which is what Git for Windows does out
# of the installer, `core.autocrlf=true` — moves that hash, and the policy then
# blocks the app's own script. Nothing says so until a packaged build flashes
# the wrong palette on launch, which is the failure `renderer-csp.test.ts`
# exists to catch and the reason this file is not merely tidiness.
#
# Normalising everything is simpler than remembering which files are
# load-bearing. `text=auto` still leaves anything Git detects as binary alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
